OpenOLMS — Authors and Credits

Author / maintainer:
  Antonio Rico / verta1878  (github.com/verta1878)

Team:
  sysop/0      — compiler (fpc264irc), FOSSIL socket backend (m_fossil_socket),
                  fpc264irc Wine deadlock fix (InitSystemThreads), PPU rebuild
  wrench       — binary compatibility (OL_Compat.pas, L1-L7), message editor,
                  user configuration, upgrade tools, serial layer (serial_ext.pas),
                  protocol analyzer (NM_DebugView), engine architecture
  kiddo        — serial IRQ ring buffer, protocol stack (Zmodem Int64 fix,
                  Ymodem batch, Xmodem 1K/CRC, Kermit sliding window)
  evga         — display, RIPView, SIO2K OS/2 driver rebuild (13,371 lines),
                  Mystic BBS monitor
  hexadecimal  — PCBoard 15.4 (pcbrevival), Linux serial plan (ASYNC mapping),
                  pcbis installer UI, PCBTIC, BinkleyTerm XE mailer plan
  g00r00       — Mystic BBS protocol code (Copyright 1997-2013 James Coyle, GPLv3)

Original OLMS:
  Peter Rocca  — OLMS Version 2000 (MCC, 1994-1998)
                  Permission granted July 2026, GPLv3.
                  Clean-room reimplementation — no original source code used.
                  All record layouts reverse-engineered from published data files.

Built from published format specifications:
  QWK        — Mark "Sparky" Herring
  QWKE       — community extension spec
  Blue Wave  — Cutting Edge Computing
  JAM        — Joaquim Homrighausen, Andrew Adams, Mats Lentz, Mats Wittel
  Hudson     — QuickBBS / RemoteAccess community format

Binary compatibility verified against OLMS Version 2000 data files:
  OLMS.CFG (14,889 bytes), USERS.DAT (30 × 478), MESSAGES.CTL (383 × 64)
